main: create the keyboard on the bottom layer

The keyboard's surface is created on the overlay layer, whose exclusive
zone a compositor places before the bottom layer's. A docked swaybar is
on the bottom layer, so it moves above the keyboard each time the
keyboard is shown.

Create the keyboard on the bottom layer. The bar then keeps the screen
edge and the keyboard takes its space above the bar.

---
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -61,1 +61,1 @@
-static uint32_t layer = ZWLR_LAYER_SHELL_V1_LAYER_OVERLAY;
+static uint32_t layer = ZWLR_LAYER_SHELL_V1_LAYER_BOTTOM;
